title = "comp-goalrun/comp-goald — a REFUSED gate must not read as success"

text = """
Fix a real bug found running the daemon live: `comp-goalrun`'s exit code
cannot currently distinguish "a branch won" from "the gate refused to run,
nothing was spent." Both are exit 0. `comp-goald` only checks
`status.success()`, so a REFUSED goal (its own `[[check]].command` wasn't in
the tree yet, or every check already passes on the untouched base) gets
reported to the platform as `awaiting-human` — a pull request waiting for
review — when no branch ever ran and nothing was opened. This is not
theoretical: it happened while testing this exact pipeline tonight.

This is a NATIVE Rust fix inside `reconciler/`, not a wasm component — there
is no WIT world, no `cargo component`, no HTTP gate here. The judge is a
plain `cargo test`.

## What to build

**A new file, `reconciler/src/goalexit.rs`**, a small self-contained module
with exactly these public items (the held-out test in `context` below
depends on these exact names — read it, it is the literal specification):

  - `pub const SUCCESS: i32 = 0;` — the OS's own convention; `comp-goald`'s
    `status.success()` check depends on this staying 0.
  - `pub const EXHAUSTED: i32 = 3;` — comp-goalrun's EXISTING exit code for
    "every branch ran, none passed the gate" (already used at
    `std::process::exit(3)` in `reconciler/src/bin/goalrun.rs` — do not
    change that call site's value, just its meaning becomes "this module's
    EXHAUSTED constant" instead of a bare literal).
  - `pub const GATE_REFUSED: i32 = 4;` — NEW: the gate could not judge
    anything, nothing was spent. This is the code this fix introduces.
  - `pub fn failure_reason(code: Option<i32>) -> String` — given the exit
    code `comp-goalrun` returned (or `None`, meaning it was killed by a
    signal — `std::process::ExitStatus::code()` returns `None` in that
    case, and this must not panic), returns the human-readable reason
    `comp-goald` reports to the platform's `/api/goals/{id}/fail` endpoint.
    `Some(EXHAUSTED)` and `Some(GATE_REFUSED)` must produce DIFFERENT
    strings (read the held-out test for the exact substrings each must
    contain); anything else falls back to a generic message that names the
    actual numeric code, because an operator debugging a crash needs the
    number.

**`reconciler/src/lib.rs`** — add `pub mod goalexit;` to the existing module
list (alphabetical order, matching the file's own convention — it goes
after `pub mod generation;` and before `pub mod memory;`). Change NOTHING
else in this file; it is shown to you in full in `context` below.

**`reconciler/src/bin/goalrun.rs`** — find the `ponytail:` comment near
`gate_can_judge`'s call site (search for `gate_can_judge(&goal`). Currently:

    if !gate_can_judge(&goal, &checks, &gate, &base_commit, &tree, args.timeout) {
        return Ok(());
    }

Change the body of that `if` to exit with the new distinct code instead of
returning success:

    if !gate_can_judge(&goal, &checks, &gate, &base_commit, &tree, args.timeout) {
        std::process::exit(comp_reconciler::goalexit::GATE_REFUSED);
    }

Leave the `ponytail:` comment above it in place — it documents WHY this
line exists, and a future reader should still find it there. Do not touch
any other `return Ok(())`, `std::process::exit(3)`, or anything else in this
huge file — this is a one-line, surgical change.

**`reconciler/src/bin/goald.rs`** — in the `work` function, find the
`else` branch that computes `reason` from `status.code()`:

    let reason = match status.code() {
        Some(3) => "no branch passed the gate — the goal needs work, not a retry".to_string(),
        code => format!("comp-goalrun exited {}", code.unwrap_or(-1)),
    };

Replace the whole `let reason = ...;` statement with a call to the new
module:

    let reason = comp_reconciler::goalexit::failure_reason(status.code());

Do not change anything else in this file — the surrounding `eprintln!`,
the `call(...)` invocation, all of it stays exactly as it is.
"""

base_paths = [
  "reconciler/",
  "lattice/",
  "comp-metadata/",
]

writable = [
  "reconciler/src/goalexit.rs",
  "reconciler/src/lib.rs",
  "reconciler/src/bin/goalrun.rs",
  "reconciler/src/bin/goald.rs",
]

context = [
  # The held-out judge itself: not writable, but shown up front — it is the
  # literal specification of every name and every substring `goalexit.rs`
  # must produce, and hiding it would just buy one wasted generation of
  # guessing wrong before the gate's own error message said the same thing.
  "reconciler/tests/goalexit.rs",
]

[[check]]
id = "goalexit-behaves-correctly"
required = true
weight = 1
command = ["cargo", "test", "--release", "--manifest-path", "reconciler/Cargo.toml", "--test", "goalexit"]
